  "notes": "This focused public C++ TCK contract exercises IEEE 1516.1-2025 §4.1.7 p. 50 l. 78-25, §4.2 p. 51 l. 33-6, and §12.5 p. 356 l. 293 and l. 383-127 through Connect. The protected current-process adapter selects the standard HLAauthorizer with a global password. The TCK passes HLAnoCredentials, a wrong HLAplainTextPassword, and the matching password as Connect arguments; it requires Unauthorized for the first two and successful Connect/Disconnect for the matching password. For §4.2, this directly witnesses Connect requiring credentials with valid type and data when authorization is enabled; it does not generalize beyond Connect. The test also verifies that HLAauthorizer recognizes the predefined no-credentials type before applying its policy. Installed-package MinGW CTest and direct evidence pass in HLA_EVOKED and HLA_IMMEDIATE. This is limited to authorizeRtiOperation/Connect and is not provider conformance or full conformance evidence.",
